ype":"text_delta","text":"bank-of-canada-"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"interest-rate-october-"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"2026) exp"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"ects one more hike to 2"},{"type":"text_delta","text":".75%,"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" then a"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" more cautious approach to"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" avoid overtightening."},{"type":"text_delta","text":"\n\nI didn't find a conf"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"irmed date for the next announ"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"cement. I can"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" set"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" up"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" a scheduled al"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"ert for"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" it if you'd like."},{"type":"completed","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"opaque","provider":"anthropic","kind":"thinking","data":{"signature":"","thinking":"","type":"thinking"}},{"type":"text","text":"The Bank of Canada raised its key rate by 25 basis points to 2.5% on October 28, 2026. That is the latest decision I found.\n\n- **Rates:** The Bank Rate is now 2.75% and the deposit rate is 2.45%, according to the [Bank of Canada press release](https://www.bankofcanada.ca/2026/10/fad-press-release-2026-10-28).\n- **Context:** It is the first rate change in about a year and the first increase since July 2023. The Bank had held at 2.25% for seven straight meetings, per [CBC](https://www.cbc.ca/news/business/livestory/bank-of-canada-interest-rate-announcement-oct-28-9.7398140).\n- **Why:** High energy prices have kept CPI inflation around 3% since April. The Bank expects it to reach about 3½% by year-end. Excluding gasoline, inflation was 2.2% in September, and core measures are close to 2%. The Bank hiked to keep high energy prices from spreading to other prices.\n- **Outlook:** The Bank said more increases may be needed but that it will \"proceed carefully\". In the [press conference](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=J1KV7iYOIAI), Governor Macklem said there is no predetermined path and that decisions will be taken one meeting at a time.\n- **Analyst view:** [TD](https://stories.td.com/ca/en/article/bank-of-canada-interest-rate-october-2026) expects one more hike to 2.75%, then a more cautious approach to avoid overtightening.\n\nI didn't find a confirmed date for the next announcement. I can set up a scheduled alert for it if you'd like."}]},"stop_reason":"end_turn","usage":{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":615,"cache_read_input_tokens":7651,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0},"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","refusal_category":null}]}
